Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Spike: end-to-end live decision loop run (Wikipedia goal
 + click-only isolation)

Wires the already-proven CDP-attach and Claude-CLI text adapter into one
live Agent.run() against a real TypeSafe decision loop: the README Wikipedia
goal (TYPE_TEXT + CLICK, reached goal in ~9.3s, 5 decisions/2 actions) and a
click-only goal on the same site to isolate Jev latency from text-model
latency (~4.8s, 3 decisions/1 action, no TYPE_TEXT). Adds the small Chromium
launch script used to drive both runs. Verdict recorded in SPIKE-NOTES.md:
Jev latency is fast (300-1100ms/decision) but the Claude-CLI TYPE_TEXT step
(~4.8s/call) dominates any typing-heavy flow.
